            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">7 · Mobile fullscreen (multiple)</h3>
              <Autocomplete id="ds-ac-fs" label="Experiences" placeholder="Search experiences…" selectionMode="multiple" mobileMode="fullscreen" options={acExperiences} help="Below 768px this opens a fullscreen search with a Done button." />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">Adaptive on mobile (default)</h3>
              <Autocomplete id="ds-ac-adaptive" label="Country" placeholder="Search countries…" options={countries} help="Dropdown while there is room; fullscreen when the keyboard or viewport leaves under 200px." />
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-5">States</h3>
          <form class="row g-4 mt-0" id="ds-ac-form" novalidate>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <Autocomplete id="ds-ac-required" label="Required" placeholder="Choose a country" options={plainCountries} name="required-country" required validateOnBlur invalidFeedback="Please choose a country." />
              <button type="submit" class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm mt-3">Submit form</button>
              <span class="small text-ink-soft ms-2" id="ds-ac-form-out"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <Autocomplete id="ds-ac-disabled" label="Disabled" options={plainCountries} defaultValue="fr" disabled />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <Autocomplete id="ds-ac-readonly" label="Readonly" options={plainCountries} defaultValue="jp" readonly />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <Autocomplete id="ds-ac-popular" label="Recent &amp; popular" placeholder="Search countries…" options={countries} showPopular showRecent help="With no query: Recent (this session), then Popular." />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <Autocomplete id="ds-ac-loading" label="Loading" placeholder="Search…" options={plainCountries} state="loading" />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <Autocomplete id="ds-ac-error" label="Error" placeholder="Search…" options={plainCountries} state="error" />
            </div>
          </form>

          <p class="small text-ink-soft mt-4 mb-0">
            Event log: <span id="ds-ac-log">nothing yet</span>
          </p>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-5">Props</h3>
          <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-sm small align-middle">
              <thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Default</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>options</code></td><td>required</td><td><code>&#123; value, label, secondaryLabel?, image?, imageAlt?, icon?, disabled?, …meta &#125;</code>. Any extra keys are kept and returned in events.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>label</code> / <code>ariaLabel</code></td><td>—</td><td>One is required for an accessible name.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>selectionMode</code></td><td><code>single</code></td><td><code>single | multiple</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>selectedVisual</code></td><td><code>none</code></td><td><code>none | leading</code>. Single select only: <code>leading</code> shows the selected option's <code>image</code> / <code>icon</code> before the input, using the same visual as its list row.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>selectedDisplay</code></td><td><code>label</code></td><td><code>label | secondaryLabel</code>. Text shown in the closed control; <code>secondaryLabel</code> (e.g. a dial code) falls back to the label when an option has none. The list always shows labels, and the full label is exposed via <code>aria-describedby</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>value</code> / <code>defaultValue</code></td><td>—</td><td>String, or string[] for multiple. Values are looked up in <code>options</code>; for remote data use <code>setValue(values, optionObjects)</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>name</code></td><td>—</td><td>Submitted via hidden inputs (one per value; repeated name for multiple).</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>maxSelections</code></td><td>none</td><td>Multiple only. Disabled options never count.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>maxVisibleChips</code></td><td>all</td><td>Extra chips collapse to a “+N” button.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>disabled</code> / <code>readonly</code> / <code>required</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Required is validated natively and shown with Bootstrap's <code>is-invalid</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>clearable</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>“Clear selection” button, single select only (multi-select removes items via chips); locked (disabled + selected) items stay.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>state</code></td><td><code>ready</code></td><td><code>ready | loading | error</code> — replaces a <code>loading</code> boolean (project rule: enums, not booleans). “Empty” is derived from the results.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>searchUrl</code></td><td>—</td><td>GET <code>url?q=…</code> returning an options array. For anything else call <code>setSource((query, &#123; signal &#125;) =&gt; Promise&lt;options[]&gt;)</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>debounce</code> / <code>minSearchLength</code></td><td><code>250</code> / <code>0</code></td><td>Remote only. Stale requests are aborted; results are cached per query.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>openOnFocus</code> · <code>autoFocus</code></td><td><code>true</code> · <code>false</code></td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>closeOnSelect</code></td><td>single <code>true</code> · multiple <code>false</code></td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>closeOnEscape</code> · <code>closeOnOutsideClick</code> · <code>closeOnBack</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>toggleOnEnter</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Multiple: Enter on a selected option deselects it.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>backspaceRemovesLast</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Only when the query is empty.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>wrapNavigation</code> · <code>pageNavigation</code></td><td><code>false</code> · <code>true</code></td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>validateOnBlur</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>placement</code></td><td><code>auto</code></td><td><code>auto | top | bottom</code>. Auto opens below unless there is more room above.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>positionStrategy</code></td><td><code>adaptive</code></td><td><code>adaptive | absolute | fixed</code>. Adaptive uses <code>fixed</code> when an ancestor clips overflow.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>maxHeight</code></td><td><code>auto</code></td><td><code>auto</code> = available room, capped at 22rem; or a number (px) / CSS length.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>mobileMode</code></td><td><code>adaptive</code></td><td><code>adaptive | dropdown | fullscreen</code>. No bottom sheet.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>keyboardAware</code> · <code>viewportAware</code> · <code>safeAreaAware</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>See “Mobile”.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>lockBodyScroll</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Fullscreen only.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>showApplyButton</code> · <code>applyLabel</code></td><td><code>true</code> · <code>Done</code></td><td>Multiple + fullscreen only.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>inputMode</code> · <code>enterKeyHint</code></td><td><code>search</code> · <code>done</code> (<code>search</code> when remote)</td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>highlightMatch</code> · <code>showRecent</code> · <code>showPopular</code></td><td><code>true</code> · <code>false</code> · <code>false</code></td><td>Popular uses <code>popular: true</code> on options; Recent is per page load (<code>setRecent()</code> to seed).</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>labels</code></td><td>English</td><td>Override any string (<code>empty</code>, <code>loading</code>, <code>error</code>, <code>retry</code>, <code>remove</code>, <code>limitReached</code>…).</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Events</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-soft small">
            Bubbling <code>CustomEvent</code>s on the root, named <code>autocomplete:&lt;name&gt;</code> (the
            spec's <code>onX</code> callbacks): <code>change</code>, <code>select</code>, <code>remove</code>,
            <code>clear</code>, <code>search</code>, <code>input</code>, <code>focus</code>, <code>blur</code>,
            <code>open</code>, <code>close</code>, <code>fullscreen</code>, <code>error</code>. <code>detail</code> on
            change: <code>value, values, options, count, max, remaining, limitReached, reason</code> — enough to render
            “You can select up to 3 items” (example 4 does).
          </p>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Behaviour</h3>
          <ul class="text-ink-soft small">
            <li><strong>Active ≠ selected ≠ disabled.</strong> Arrow keys and hover only highlight; only Enter, click or tap commits. The query is never the value: after searching “United”, the selection is unchanged until you pick another option, and the input reverts to it on close.</li>
            <li><strong>Selection limit.</strong> At the limit, unselected options stay visible, dimmed, <code>aria-disabled</code> with a “Selection limit reached” cue; chips stay removable and removing one frees a slot. Mouse, touch, keyboard and Enter all respect it.</li>
            <li><strong>Disabled options</strong> stay visible, struck through with a block icon, are skipped by arrows/Home/End/Page keys, and can never be selected. A selected + disabled option is a locked chip: no remove button, not cleared, not counted.</li>
            <li><strong>Keys.</strong> ↓/↑ move (↓ on a closed list opens it); Home/End jump when navigating the list, and move the caret while you are editing text; PageUp/PageDown move a page; Enter selects the highlighted option and never submits the form (with nothing highlighted it is left alone, so the form submits); Esc closes; Tab/Shift+Tab close without selecting and move focus normally; Backspace on an empty query removes the last chip.</li>
            <li><strong>Remote.</strong> Loading keeps previous results visible but inert; error shows “Unable to load results” with a Try again button (Enter or ↓ also retries); minimum length shows a hint instead of an empty state.</li>
            <li><strong>Mobile.</strong> Adaptive: below 768px (or a short touch screen) the list is a dropdown while at least 200px fits above or below the field, measured on <code>visualViewport</code> (which excludes the keyboard and browser chrome); otherwise the field becomes a fullscreen search in place. The input is not recreated, so focus and the keyboard survive the switch. Fullscreen locks page scroll, makes the page inert, respects safe areas, closes on Back (history entry), Esc, the back arrow or Done, and returns focus to the field without reopening the list.</li>
            <li><strong>Accessibility.</strong> <code>role=combobox</code> with <code>aria-expanded/controls/activedescendant/autocomplete</code>; <code>role=listbox</code> (<code>aria-multiselectable</code>); options with <code>aria-selected</code>/<code>aria-disabled</code>; a polite live region announces result counts, loading, errors, limit and selection changes; chips have “Remove &#123;label&#125;” buttons; the “+N” button lists what it hides.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- ================= PHONE NUMBER ================= -->
        <section id="phone-number" class="pb-6 mb-6 border-bottom">
          <h2>Phone Number</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft">
            <code>PhoneNumber.astro</code> — a country / calling-code picker beside a phone-number input, behaving as
            <strong>one</strong> form control with <strong>one</strong> value: the E.164 string (<code>+13024148567</code>).
            The picker is Autocomplete's <code>embedded</code> variant, so search, keyboard, positioning and mobile
            fullscreen are shared, not copied. Status: experimental (this page is its only use).
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-soft small">
            Modal and offcanvas behaviour is exercised on the
            <a href={`${base}/design-system/component-testing/`}>Component Testing</a> QA page.
          </p>

          <div class="row g-4 mt-1">
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">1 · Default</h3>
              <PhoneNumber id="ds-ph-default" label="Phone number" help="Pick a country, or type a full number starting with +." />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">2 · With a value and popular countries</h3>
              <PhoneNumber id="ds-ph-value" label="Phone number" value="+13024148567" popularCountries={['IN', 'US', 'GB']} name="phone-value" />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">3 · Required, inside a form</h3>
              <form id="ds-ph-form" novalidate>
                <PhoneNumber id="ds-ph-required" label="Phone number" name="phone" required help="This field is required to verify your account." />
                <div class="mt-3"><Button variant="primary" type="submit">Send code</Button></div>
              </form>
              <p class="small text-ink-soft mt-2 mb-0">Form data: <code id="ds-ph-form-out">not submitted</code></p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">4 · Live value</h3>
              <PhoneNumber id="ds-ph-live" label="Phone number" defaultCountry="US" />
              <p class="small text-ink-soft mt-2 mb-0">
                <code>getDetails()</code>: <code id="ds-ph-live-out">{'{}'}</code>
              </p>
              <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-2">
                <Button variant="secondary" id="ds-ph-live-set">setValue(+919876543210)</Button>
                <Button variant="secondary" id="ds-ph-live-invalid">showInvalid()</Button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">5 · Disabled</h3>
              <PhoneNumber id="ds-ph-disabled" label="Phone number" value="+13024148567" disabled />
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-5">Props</h3>
          <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-sm small align-middle">
              <thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Default</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>label</code> / <code>ariaLabel</code></td><td>— / <code>Phone number</code></td><td>The group is named by <code>label</code>, or <code>ariaLabel</code> when there is none.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>name</code></td><td>—</td><td>Names the single hidden input that carries the E.164 value. The country picker and the number input are never named.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>value</code> / <code>defaultValue</code></td><td>—</td><td>One E.164 string. The country and the national number are both derived from it; an invalid string is ignored.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>defaultCountry</code></td><td><code>IN</code></td><td>ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 region used when there is no value.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>popularCountries</code></td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>ISO codes pinned in a “Popular” group above the full list.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>placeholder</code></td><td>example number</td><td>Defaults to an example mobile number for the selected country, e.g. <code>(201) 555-0123</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>help</code></td><td>—</td><td>Help text under the field.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>required</code> / <code>disabled</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Required is enforced on the closest form's submit (a hidden input is skipped by native validation). Callers without a form call <code>showInvalid()</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>labels</code></td><td>English</td><td><code>country</code>, <code>required</code>, <code>invalid</code>, <code>tooShort</code>, <code>tooLong</code>.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Value contract</h3>
          <ul class="text-ink-soft small">
            <li><strong>One value.</strong> Read it with <code>getPhoneNumber(el).getValue()</code> or from the hidden input: <code>+13024148567</code>. It is <code>""</code> while the number is empty, incomplete or invalid, so a half-typed number can never be submitted.</li>
            <li><strong>Structured.</strong> <code>getDetails()</code> returns <code>&#123; value, country, dialCode, national, isValid, isEmpty &#125;</code>. <code>setValue(e164)</code> restores both inputs; <code>setCountry(iso)</code> changes the country and re-formats the digits already typed.</li>
            <li><strong>Events.</strong> <code>phone-number:change</code> (bubbling <code>CustomEvent</code>, <code>detail</code> = <code>getDetails()</code> + <code>instance</code>) fires when the country or the E.164 value changes; the hidden input also fires a native <code>change</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>International entry.</strong> Typing or pasting <code>+44 …</code> switches the country. A code that is still ambiguous (<code>+1</code>) leaves the current country alone.</li>
            <li><strong>Reset.</strong> <code>form.reset()</code> restores the initial value.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Behaviour</h3>
          <ul class="text-ink-soft small">
            <li><strong>Country list.</strong> Search matches the name, the ISO code and the calling code (“united”, “us”, “44”, “+44”). Choosing a country moves focus to the number.</li>
            <li><strong>Formatting.</strong> The number formats as you type (never while deleting, and only with the caret at the end) and settles on the national format when the field loses focus with a valid number.</li>
            <li><strong>Validation.</strong> Shown on blur for a non-empty invalid number, and on submit for an empty required one. The message says whether the number is too short or too long; the valid state adds a check icon, so meaning never rests on colour alone.</li>
            <li><strong>Accessibility.</strong> The field is a <code>role="group"</code> named by the label. The picker is a combobox named “Country code” (the selected country's full name is announced too); the number is <code>type="tel"</code> with <code>autocomplete="tel-national"</code>; the message is <code>role="alert"</code> and referenced by <code>aria-describedby</code> with <code>aria-invalid</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>States.</strong> Default, focus, error, success and disabled are built. Loading, skeleton and empty are not: the country data is bundled at build time and the field has no remote content. Hover: none beyond Autocomplete's list rows.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-ink-soft small">
            Flags are 4:3 SVGs from <code>flag-icons</code> in <code>public/flags</code>, loaded lazily. Validation uses
            <code>libphonenumber-js</code> (minimal metadata).
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- ================= DATE & TIME SLOT PICKER ================= -->
        <section id="date-time-slot-picker" class="pb-6 mb-6 border-bottom">
          <h2>Date &amp; Time Slot Picker</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft">
            <code>DateTimeSlotPicker.astro</code> — single date + single time-slot selector, in two
            presentations: an inline <code>bootstrap.Collapse</code> panel embedded in its own container, or a
            <code>bootstrap.Modal</code> the component owns end to end. There is no third mode and no
            nested-modal support (<code>autoDetectModal</code>/<code>zIndex</code> props) by design — a
            picker triggered from inside another modal should use <code>presentation="inline"</code> instead.
            Status: experimental (this page is its only use).
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-soft small">
            Container-context scenarios (inline mode's Collapse panel inside a scrollable modal body and an
            offcanvas body) are exercised on the
            <a href={`${base}/design-system/component-testing/`}>Component Testing</a> QA page.
          </p>

          <div class="row g-4 mt-1">
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">1 · Modal (default)</h3>
              <DateTimeSlotPicker id="ds-dtsp-modal" availability={dtspAvailability} />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">2 · Inline</h3>
              <DateTimeSlotPicker id="ds-dtsp-inline" presentation="inline" availability={dtspAvailability} />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">3 · Disabled dates</h3>
              <DateTimeSlotPicker
                id="ds-dtsp-disabled-dates"
                availability={dtspAvailability}
                disabledDates={[dtspHoliday]}
                triggerDescription="Closed Fridays, plus one holiday"
              />
              <p class="form-text">
                The holiday ({dtspHoliday}) comes from <code>disabledDates</code>; every Friday is closed via
                a <code>setDateDisabledRule()</code> call after hydration (<code>isDateDisabled</code> can't be
                a prop — see below).
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">4 · No availability / fully booked</h3>
              <DateTimeSlotPicker id="ds-dtsp-availability" availability={dtspAvailability} triggerDescription="Try the 4th and 6th dates in the strip" />
              <p class="form-text">Date index 3 is closed (no slots); date index 5 is fully booked (every slot taken).</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-5">States</h3>
          <form class="row g-4 mt-0" id="ds-dtsp-form" novalidate>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <DateTimeSlotPicker id="ds-dtsp-required" label="Booking Time (modal + required)" required name="Booking" availability={dtspAvailability} />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <DateTimeSlotPicker id="ds-dtsp-required-inline" presentation="inline" label="Booking Time (inline + required)" required name="BookingInline" availability={dtspAvailability} />
            </div>
            <div class="col-12">
              <button type="submit" class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm">Submit form</button>
              <span class="small text-ink-soft ms-2" id="ds-dtsp-form-out"></span>
              <p class="form-text mb-0">
                Submit with nothing selected to see the invalid state. Inline, the whole control turns
                invalid as one: the root gets <code>dtsp--invalid</code>, the panel border goes red, the trigger's
                bottom edge stays open when expanded so trigger + panel read as a single red field, and the
                message renders <em>below the panel</em>, linked to the trigger with <code>aria-describedby</code>
                (plus <code>aria-invalid</code>). It clears itself as soon as a valid slot is committed.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <DateTimeSlotPicker id="ds-dtsp-disabled" availability={dtspAvailability} disabled />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <DateTimeSlotPicker id="ds-dtsp-loading" availability={dtspAvailability} loading />
            </div>
          </form>

          <p class="small text-ink-soft mt-4 mb-0">
            Event log: <span id="ds-dtsp-log">nothing yet</span>
          </p>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-5">Props</h3>
          <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-sm small align-middle">
              <thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Default</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>presentation</code></td><td><code>modal</code></td><td><code>modal | inline</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>showHeader</code> · <code>showFooter</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Modal only — the recorded inline panel has no title bar or footer.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>label</code> · <code>modalSubtitle</code></td><td>“Select Date &amp; Time” · “Choose an available slot for your booking”</td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>minDate</code> · <code>maxDate</code></td><td><code>today</code> · <code>+30days</code></td><td>Literal <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code> or a relative <code>±Ndays</code> string.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>initialDate</code></td><td>—</td><td>A disabled value is a config error: falls back to the first enabled date in range and logs a warning.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>dateFormat</code></td><td><code>ddd, MMM D</code></td><td>Split on the first comma for the date-strip pill's two lines; used whole for the trigger's summary line.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>disabledDates</code></td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>Explicit blackout dates. For a recurring rule (e.g. “every Friday”), call <code>getDateTimeSlotPicker(el).setDateDisabledRule(date =&gt; boolean)</code> after hydration — a function can't be a prop on a build-time component.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>timeFormat</code></td><td><code>12h</code></td><td><code>12h | 24h</code> — display only; the payload's <code>value.time</code> is always 24h.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>showPeriodGroups</code> · <code>showPeriodTimeRange</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Morning/Afternoon/Evening headers and their “(8:00 AM – 11:30 AM)” range, computed from that date's actual slots.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>value</code> / <code>defaultValue</code></td><td>—</td><td>A full payload (see “Payload” below) — controlled / initial committed selection.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>requireConfirmation</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Modal: gates the Apply button. Inline: gates closing via the trigger (there's no separate Apply affordance inline). <code>false</code> commits on slot click instead.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>resetTimeOnDateChange</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Changing the date clears the in-progress time selection, never the already-committed value.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>triggerLabel</code> · <code>triggerDescription</code></td><td>“Select Date &amp; Time” · “Choose an available slot”</td><td>Shown until a selection is committed, then replaced by the summary + “Click to edit”.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>closeOnEscape</code> · <code>closeOnOutsideClick</code></td><td><code>true</code> · <code>false</code></td><td>Modal only — <code>keyboard</code> / <code>backdrop:'static'</code>. Always free of the selection-required gate.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>required</code> / <code>disabled</code> / <code>loading</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Required enforces on the closest <code>&lt;form&gt;</code>'s submit (the value carrier is a <code>type="hidden"</code> input, which native constraint validation can't target). Callers that don't use native form submission (e.g. a stepper's Continue button) call <code>getDateTimeSlotPicker(el).showInvalid()</code> instead; <code>clearInvalid()</code> resets it and a committed value clears it automatically. Loading skeletons the trigger.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>availability</code></td><td><code>[]</code></td><td><code>&#123; date, status?, slots: [&#123; id, time, label, status &#125;] &#125;[]</code>. Slot times/labels are never hard-coded by the component.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>name</code></td><td>—</td><td>Hidden input value = <code>value.datetimeLocal</code> (native <code>datetime-local</code> format).</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Payload</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-soft small">
            One payload on <code>change</code>/<code>apply</code> covers native inputs, DB columns and display
            text at once: <code>value.&#123;date, time, datetimeLocal&#125;</code> (DATE/TIME/<code>datetime-local</code>
            formats), <code>slot.&#123;id, status, group&#125;</code>, and
            <code>display.&#123;date, time, combined&#125;</code> (e.g. <code>"Sep 24, 2026 · 7:00 PM"</code>).
          </p>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Events</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-soft small">
            Bubbling <code>CustomEvent</code>s on the root, named <code>dtsp:&lt;name&gt;</code> (the spec's
            <code>onX</code> callbacks): <code>open</code>, <code>close</code>, <code>datechange</code>
            (<code>&#123;date, previousDate&#125;</code>), <code>slotselect</code> (<code>&#123;slotId, time&#125;</code>),
            <code>change</code> / <code>apply</code> (the full payload above), <code>cancel</code>,
            <code>clear</code> (<code>&#123;previousValue&#125;</code>).
          </p>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Behaviour</h3>
          <ul class="text-ink-soft small">
            <li><strong>Opening is always free; closing/confirming is gated.</strong> The modal's Apply button and inline's close-via-trigger gesture both refuse to proceed without a complete date + time selection, showing “Please select a time slot(&nbsp;to continue).” in place rather than as a toast. Cancel, the modal's × button, Escape and a static backdrop always close and discard the in-progress draft back to the last committed value — required selection never traps a guest who just wants to back out.</li>
            <li><strong>Selected date and selected slot share one visual</strong> (solid dark fill, light text) — not two separate “selected” styles.</li>
            <li><strong>Booked ≠ past ≠ disabled.</strong> A booked slot is muted <em>and</em> struck through; a date excluded by <code>disabledDates</code>/<code>setDateDisabledRule</code>/the min–max window is muted with no strikethrough and carries a real “Full”/unavailable label rather than colour alone.</li>
            <li><strong>Keys.</strong> On the date strip and the slot grid: ←/→ move between enabled items (disabled ones are skipped entirely, never focused); Home/End jump to the first/last enabled item; ↑/↓ move between the Morning/Afternoon/Evening groups in the slot grid; Enter/Space selects; Esc closes only this picker (in inline mode, never a parent modal it happens to sit inside).</li>
            <li><strong>Accessibility.</strong> Date and slot items use <code>role="option"</code>/<code>aria-selected</code>/<code>aria-disabled</code>; the modal has <code>aria-labelledby</code>, the inline panel <code>role="group"</code>; one polite live region announces date/slot changes and validation text, separate from the always-in-DOM validation row itself.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- ================= DATE PICKER ================= -->
        <section id="date-picker" class="pb-6 mb-6 border-bottom">
          <h2>Date Picker</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft">
            <code>DatePicker.astro</code> — one calendar date, availability-aware. The field is a
            <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> that opens an anchored, <em>non-modal</em> dropdown panel with a single
            Monday-first month grid; a hidden input carries the value as a plain <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code> string
            (or <code>''</code>). One presentation on every screen size — no full-screen sheet, no inert
            background, no scroll lock. Selecting a date commits immediately and closes the panel (no Apply).
            Status: experimental (this page is its only use).
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-soft small">
            Dates are strings and all arithmetic is integer day numbers (<code>scripts/date-only.js</code>);
            only <code>todayISO()</code> reads the clock, in <code>Asia/Muscat</code>, so a timezone can never
            shift a selected date. The panel is <code>position: fixed</code> and placed against the
            <em>visual</em> viewport, so it is never clipped by an overflow ancestor. The modal and offcanvas
            scenarios are on the
            <a href={`${base}/design-system/component-testing/`}>Component Testing</a> QA page.
          </p>

          <div class="row g-4 mt-1">
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">1 · Default</h3>
              <DatePicker id="ds-dp-basic" label="Arrival date" name="arrival" help="Any date from today for the next 365 days." />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">2 · Preset value + blackout dates</h3>
              <DatePicker id="ds-dp-preset" label="Visit date" name="visit" value={dpPreset} blackoutDates={dpBlackouts} help="The next three days are blacked out (faded, not struck through)." />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">3 · Availability source (async)</h3>
              <DatePicker id="ds-dp-source" label="Lodge date" name="lodge" help="Loaded per month with a ~1s delay. Every 5th day is unavailable; some days are missing from the response (unknown). Month +2 fails once — use Retry." />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">4 · min / max window</h3>
              <DatePicker id="ds-dp-window" label="Workshop date" minDate={dpMin} maxDate={dpMax} placeholder="Pick a date this fortnight" help="minDate and maxDate are themselves selectable." />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">5 · Year selection (5-year window)</h3>
              <DatePicker id="ds-dp-years" label="Event date" name="event" maxDate={dpFarMax} help="Click the month title to jump between years." />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h3 class="h6">6 · Legend (legend="show")</h3>
              <DatePicker id="ds-dp-legend" label="Stay date" name="stay" legend="show" help="The key is hidden by default." />
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-5">States</h3>
          <div class="row g-4 mt-0">
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h4 class="h6 text-ink-soft">Invalid (initial error)</h4>
              <DatePicker id="ds-dp-error" label="Booking date" error="Please choose a booking date." help="Help text stays in the description." />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h4 class="h6 text-ink-soft">Disabled</h4>
              <DatePicker id="ds-dp-disabled" label="Booking date" disabled />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h4 class="h6 text-ink-soft">No visible label (aria-label)</h4>
              <DatePicker id="ds-dp-aria" ariaLabel="Departure date" />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h4 class="h6 text-ink-soft">Programmatic</h4>
              <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                <Button variant="secondary" class="btn-sm" id="ds-dp-set">setValue(+7 days)</Button>
                <Button variant="secondary" class="btn-sm" id="ds-dp-clear">clear()</Button>
                <Button variant="secondary" class="btn-sm" id="ds-dp-disable">Toggle disabled</Button>
              </div>
              <p class="form-text mb-0">Drives the “Default” picker above. <code>setValue()</code> is silent; <code>clear()</code> emits <code>change</code> only if there was a value.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="small text-ink-soft mt-4 mb-0">
            Event log: <span id="ds-dp-log">nothing yet</span>
          </p>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-5">State audit</h3>
          <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-sm small align-middle">
              <thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Field</th><th>Day</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>default</td><td>yes</td><td>yes (available)</td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td>hover</td><td>—</td><td>yes</td><td>Field uses Bootstrap's own; unavailable days never highlight.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>focus</td><td>yes</td><td>yes</td><td>Project focus ring; roving tab stop (one <code>tabindex="0"</code>).</td></tr>
                <tr><td>active / selected</td><td>—</td><td>yes</td><td>Fill + bold, plus <code>aria-selected</code> on the cell.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>disabled</td><td>yes</td><td>yes</td><td><em>Day:</em> <code>aria-disabled</code> (still navigable), faded, not-allowed. Blackout, past and out-of-window days.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>loading</td><td>no</td><td>month</td><td>Field is never busy — only the visible month (skeleton, <code>aria-busy</code>).</td></tr>
                <tr><td>skeleton</td><td>no</td><td>yes</td><td>Correct week count, six weeks of height reserved, no spinner (known layout).</td></tr>
                <tr><td>empty</td><td>n.a.</td><td>n.a.</td><td>A month always has days; a missing availability entry is <code>unknown</code>, not empty.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>error</td><td>yes (invalid)</td><td>month</td><td>Field: Bootstrap invalid state. Month: inline “Couldn't load availability” + Retry (no toast).</td></tr>
                <tr><td>success</td><td>no</td><td>no</td><td>Selecting closes the panel; no separate success treatment.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Props</h3>
          <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-sm small align-middle">
              <thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Default</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>label</code> · <code>ariaLabel</code></td><td>—</td><td>With a label the field is named <code>aria-labelledby="label value"</code>; without, <code>ariaLabel</code>, then <code>placeholder</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>id</code> · <code>name</code></td><td>random <code>drp-…</code> · —</td><td><code>name</code> goes on the hidden input. Every generated id is derived from <code>id</code>, so instances never collide.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>placeholder</code></td><td>“Select a date”</td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>help</code></td><td>—</td><td>Renders <code>.form-text</code>, included in the field's description. Omitted entirely when absent.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>error</code></td><td>—</td><td>Mounts invalid (<code>.is-invalid</code>, <code>aria-invalid</code>, Bootstrap's <code>.invalid-feedback</code>) and fires <code>dp:invalid</code> once. Bootstrap's validation icon is suppressed — the calendar icon sits there.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>value</code> · <code>defaultValue</code></td><td><code>null</code></td><td><code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>; anything that isn't a real calendar date (e.g. <code>2026-02-30</code>) silently becomes empty.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>disabled</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>minDate</code> · <code>maxDate</code></td><td>today · today + 365 days</td><td>Both are themselves selectable. Past dates are never selectable, whatever <code>minDate</code> says.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>yearSelection</code></td><td><code>auto</code></td><td><code>auto | off</code>. <code>auto</code>: the month title opens a year grid whenever the window spans more than one calendar year (a one-year window has nothing to choose, so the title stays a plain heading). <code>off</code> always keeps the plain heading.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>legend</code></td><td><code>hide</code></td><td><code>show | hide</code>. <code>show</code> renders the Available / Selected / Unavailable key under the month grid (not shown in the year view).</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>blackoutDates</code></td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>Rendered disabled (faded, not struck through).</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Methods</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-soft small">
            <code>getDatePicker(el)</code> returns the controller (<code>el</code> is the root or any child):
            <code>open()</code>, <code>close()</code>, <code>clear()</code>, <code>setValue(v)</code>,
            <code>setRules(&#123;today, minDate, maxDate, blackoutDates&#125;)</code>, <code>setSource(fn)</code>,
            <code>setDisabled(bool)</code>, <code>focus()</code>, <code>getValue()</code>.
            <code>setSource(fn)</code>: <code>fn('YYYY-MM')</code> returns a Promise of
            <code>&#123; 'YYYY-MM-DD': 'available' | 'booked' | 'disabled' &#125;</code> or
            <code>[&#123; date, status &#125;]</code>. Only months intersecting the window are fetched, each once
            (cached); no source at all means every in-window date is available, while a date missing from a
            loaded month is <code>unknown</code> — never assumed available. <code>setRules()</code> that rules out
            the committed value clears it and emits <code>change</code> with <code>reason: "rules"</code>.
          </p>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Events</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-soft small">
            Bubbling <code>CustomEvent</code>s on the root, <code>dp:&lt;name&gt;</code>:
            <code>change</code> (<code>&#123;value, reason&#125;</code>, reason <code>select</code> · <code>clear</code> · <code>rules</code>),
            <code>open</code>, <code>close</code>, and <code>invalid</code> — reserved for the initial <code>error</code> prop.
            Tapping a booked/unknown/disabled day never fires <code>invalid</code>.
          </p>

          <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Behaviour</h3>
          <ul class="text-ink-soft small">
            <li><strong>Wording.</strong> An unavailable date is “unavailable” everywhere — messages, day labels (“Sunday, 18 October 2026, today, unavailable”), codes' reasons. The word “booked” is internal only.</li>
            <li><strong>Tapping a day.</strong> Disabled/unknown: nothing happens (focus stays, day stays <code>aria-disabled</code>). Booked: inline “That date is unavailable.” (<code>role="alert"</code>), still no event. Available: announce, commit, emit <code>change</code>, close.</li>
            <li><strong>Year selection.</strong> The month title is a button (<code>aria-expanded</code>, chevron flips) that swaps the grid for a 4-column list of the years the window touches — same height as the month, so the panel doesn't jump; the nav arrows and legend step aside. Choosing a year keeps the month and day where the window allows (29 Feb → 28 Feb; a month before the window's first month lands on that first month), returns to the dates, announces the new month and focuses the day. Keys in the list: ←/→ ±1 · ↑/↓ ±4 · Home/End first/last · PageUp/PageDown ±12 · Enter/Space choose · <strong>Esc steps back to the dates</strong> (a second Esc closes the picker). In the day grid, Shift+PageUp/PageDown also move a year.</li>
            <li><strong>Keys.</strong> ←/→ ±1 day · ↑/↓ ±7 · Home/End Monday/Sunday of the week · PageUp/PageDown ±1 month (day clamped) · Enter/Space select · Esc closes and returns focus to the field. Movement clamps to the window and switches month as needed.</li>
            <li><strong>Dismissal.</strong> Outside <em>tap</em> (pointerdown + pointerup on the same target, &lt;10px travel) closes without stealing focus; a scroll or drag never closes it. Tab-out and focus landing in another control close without restoring focus; Esc and selecting restore it.</li>
            <li><strong>Placement.</strong> Prefers below; flips above when below doesn't fit and above is larger (only when the current side stops fitting — no jitter); if neither fits it takes the larger side and scrolls internally under a sticky month header. Re-measured on resize, rotation, <code>visualViewport</code> resize/scroll and ancestor scroll without touching draft, focus or month. Clamped by max(1rem, safe-area inset); a fixed page header is treated as unavailable space.</li>
            <li><strong>Inside a Bootstrap modal/offcanvas.</strong> The panel stays in the modal's DOM (portalling would fall outside Bootstrap's focus trap); <code>position: fixed</code> escapes <code>.modal-body</code> clipping. Esc closes only the picker. A tap on the modal <em>backdrop</em> while the picker is open closes only the picker — that tap's click is swallowed, so dismissing the modal takes a second tap. <code>hide.bs.modal</code> / <code>hide.bs.offcanvas</code> or removing the component closes it without restoring focus.</li>
            <li><strong>Reduced motion.</strong> Only the skeleton glow animates; it stops under <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>.</li>
          </ul>
